# Blood Spatter Analysis: "Whenever one or more creatures die, mill a card and put a bloodstain counter on this enchantment. Then
# sacrifice it if it has five or more bloodstain counters on it. When you do, return target creature card from your graveyard to your
# hand." Lightning Bolt kills one of Bot2's Memnites each of turns 3, 5, 7 and 9: four counters and four milled cards, and the
# enchantment stays. On turn 11 Pyroclasm kills the last two Memnites at once: that is one trigger, so the fifth counter and one
# card milled, not two; the Spatter is sacrificed and the reflexive trigger returns a creature card from Bot1's graveyard - the
# Memnite just milled, which was milled before the target was chosen. It is the only legal target, so none is asked for: the six dead Memnites in Bot2's graveyard are not offered.

